<p>To mull is to garble something through incompetence. When wine merchants Berry Bros. sent Richard Brinsley Sheridan a &#8220;mulled-up&#8221; bill too soon for his liking, he responded:</p>
<p>You have sent me your Bilberry,<br />
Before it is Dewberry.<br />
This is nothing but a Mulberry,<br />
And I am coming round to kick your Rasberry<br />
Until it is Blackberry<br />
and Blueberry.</p>
<p>(From <a href="https://archive.org/details/winebookwines00bell/page/76/mode/2up"><em>The Wine Book</em></a>, 1969.)</p>
